  "concept": {
    "movement": "A low, measured alternating-tripod crawl on the six visible walking legs, with the armored body steady, pincers carried in front and the tail centered above the back. The scuttle increases reach and cadence.",
    "attack": "The pincers brace and spread as the tail recoils, then unfolds into a forceful overhead sting beyond the face. The walking tips stay supported and the scorpion recovers its raised guard.",
    "death": "The armored body sinks onto the ground, walking legs curl inward, the pincers settle in front, and the tail relaxes low behind the body before a still hold."
